{
  "name": "shield-bug",
  "_about": "The green shield bug (Palomena prasina), 1.3 cm long: a flat shield -- a broad pronotum with rounded shoulders, a big triangular scutellum down the middle of the back, the wings' dark membrane tips overlapping behind it; a small flat head with dark red eyes; five-jointed antennae, the last joints reddish; a sucking beak folded under the body; finely pitted, bright green in summer, bronze in autumn. Coat: the hawthorn shield bug (green and red). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
